@startuml
title Operational intelligence - agreed target, not current runtime
left to right direction
component "Diagnostics" as diagnostics
component "Evidence, measurements\nand signals" as evidence
component "Diagnostic intelligence\nand insights" as diagnostic
component "Operational MRI:\nscopes and relationships" as mri
component "Operational dimensions:\nshared flexible taxonomy" as taxonomy
component "Dynamic evaluation:\nconfidence and priority" as evaluate
component "Narrative and presentation" as presentation
component "Shared Intelligence Trace\n(target contract)" as trace
diagnostics --> evidence
evidence --> diagnostic
diagnostic --> mri
evidence --> mri
mri --> taxonomy : classify / visualise
diagnostic --> evaluate
mri --> evaluate
evidence --> evaluate
evaluate --> presentation
diagnostics ..> trace
evidence ..> trace
diagnostic ..> trace
mri ..> trace
taxonomy ..> trace
evaluate ..> trace
presentation ..> trace
note bottom of evidence
  Preserve original evidence and provenance.
  Normalisation is optional.
end note
note bottom of mri
  Single diagnostic, team system and multi-team system
  are scopes, independent of dimension associations.
  Additional evidence is not automatic confirmation.
end note
note bottom of taxonomy
  Clarity, Performance, Leadership, Culture, Foundation.
  Hierarchical classification, not five engines.
end note
note bottom of diagnostic
  Diagnostic intelligence owns diagnostic-specific
  interpretation and retains its evidence.
  Shared evaluation is a capability, not ownership.
end note
note bottom of trace
  Pipeline stages produce records; the console
  renders them. Existing SignalTraceService is partial.
end note
@enduml
